meta {
  name: Create Public Share
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/rag/conversations/{{conversationId}}/share
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "expires_in_hours": 24,
    "custom_code": "my-custom-link",
    "emails": ["tamu@example.com"],
    "notify": true
  }
}

docs {
  Creates a read-only share of the conversation, snapshotted up to its last
  turn. Passing `emails` makes the share PRIVATE: an access token is generated,
  invitees are stored, and (with `notify: true`) invite emails are sent.

  Response: { "code": "...", "accessToken": "..." }

  - expires_in_hours: link lifetime in hours (1h - 1 year). OMIT for a
    never-expiring link. Presets: 1 | 24 | 168 | 720.
  - custom_code: optional user-chosen short code (4-32 chars: letters, digits,
    '-' or '_'). Omit for an auto-generated base62 code.
  - emails: optional invitees for a private share (max 100). Normalized
    (lowercase), deduped, and must NOT include your own email.
  - notify: send invite emails immediately (default false).
  - accessToken: non-null only for private shares — embed in invite links as
    `?invite=<accessToken>`.
  - 409 CODE_TAKEN when the custom code is already in use.
  - The snapshot is immutable: turns added or edited AFTER sharing never leak
    into the public view.
}
